msgctxt "#32052"
msgid "Use TMDbHelper cache"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32053"
msgid "When TMDbHelper is installed, use a TMDb score and the IDs it has already cached. That cache is used when this addon has no TMDb key. Titles it has not cached are requested only when a TMDb key is set. TMDbHelper does not share its own key."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32054"
msgid "OMDb requests per day"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32055"
msgid "The free OMDb key allows 1,000 requests a day, and that allowance requires the key. This addon stops at the number you set and remembers it until the next UTC day. Raise it when your key allows more. 0 keeps no local count. The run also stops when OMDb itself says the limit is reached."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32056"
msgid "Turn a provider off to leave it out of an update. Local IMDb database is the IMDb score stored on this device."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32057"
msgid "Media types"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32059"
msgid "IMDb data folder"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32060"
msgid "Local folder for the downloaded files and the SQLite index. Leave empty to use the addon data folder. About 800 MB free is needed. Your own copies of the two IMDb files can go in an import folder inside this path. An index already built somewhere else stays where it is."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32061"
msgid "Download the IMDb files now. The automatic download still runs when the data is due."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32062"
msgid "Only update missing ratings"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32063"
msgid "Leave a rating that is already stored, even when the new score has moved. Write a score only when that source is not on the item yet. The minimum change applies when this is off."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32058"
msgid "All video and the schedule update only the media types that are on. Choosing one type from the addon menu still updates that type. One item from the context menu is always updated."
msgstr ""

